nary injunction = **\u2212$25\u201330/share**; dismissal = +$7\u201310.\n5. YOSEMITE (zodasiran) readout mid-2027 \u2192 +$3\u20134/share if positive.\n6. Obesity program partnership (INHBE) \u2192 +$5\u201310/share headline.\n\n**Risks (top 5):** (1) SHTG label breadth/pricing below expectations; (2) liver-safety signal at ESC; (3) Ionis IP injunction; (4) cash runway \u22642 years \u2192 $400\u2013600M equity raise before FY29 profitability; (5) GLP-1-class competition eroding SHTG urgency.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 7.5 \u2014 CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\nCommon bear trigger with the rest of a growth-tilted book: **rate shock / risk-off**. ARWR's beta 1.294 [Aggregator] and 87% institutional ownership imply high tail correlation with IBB (\u221240% in a 2022-style tape). CVaR estimate: a 3% holding could lose \u221225% (clinical) + \u221215% (multiple) \u2192 **\u22121.2pp portfolio loss** in the worst-decile quarter \u2014 acceptable if total speculative exposure is capped at 5%.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 8 \u2014 MONITORING RULES (THESIS INTEGRITY)\n\n| KPI | Threshold | Breach action |\n|---|---|---|\n| REDEMPLO quarterly sales | \u2265$90M by Q4 FY26; \u2265$250M/q run-rate by Q3 FY27 | Below \u2192 downgrade IV \u2212$10 |\n| sNDA filing | Filed by Dec-31-2026 | Slip >6m \u2192 IV \u2212$12 |\n| ESC safety | No Gr-3/4 liver signal | Signal \u2192 IV \u2212$20, stop |\n| Ionis litigation | No injunction; no adverse claim | Injunction \u2192 exit/hedge |\n| Net cash | \u2265$1.0B through FY27E | Below \u2192 add \u2212$0.95B dilution haircut |\n| YOSEMITE | Positive mid-2027 | Negative \u2192 \u2212$0.4B SOTP |\n\n**Pre-mortem (why would this fail by 2031?):** (1) SHTG reimbursement collapsed: One-REDEMPLO pricing (orphan-priced) hit payer resistance at scale; net price fell to $50\u201370k and peak stalled at $1.2B. Early warning: gross-to-net erosion >50% reported by FY29. (2) ESC/Phase-4 revealed a liver-fat/ALT signal that narrowed the label to \"AP-history only.\" Early warning: any ALT>3\u00d7ULN cluster. (3) The platform BD engine stalled \u2014 no new deals after Madrigal; SBC dilution 8%/yr with no offsetting partnership income. Early warning: 24 months without a new licensing agreement.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 9 \u2014 RED TEAM (ADVERSARIAL)\n\n**Short thesis (same data):**\n1. Revenue quality is low: 9M26 revenue $414.5M includes ~$200\u2013250M one-time Sarepta/Madrigal payments; product revenue is still <20% of the total.\n2. Q3 FY26 net loss \u2212$194.3M (missed; EPS \u2212$1.36 vs \u2212$1.26 y/y) [Actual]; opex $245M/qtr and compounding \u2014 the $840M net cash fund only ~2 years at this burn.\n3. One-REDEMPLO pricing won't survive SHTG: payers will not pay orphan pricing for a broad metabolic population; net price will be \u2264$100k, most likely $60\u201380k.\n4. Ionis litigation: plozasiran directly threatens Tryngolza's franchise; Ionis has deep-pocket incentive to enjoin; one adverse ruling removes the core asset.\n5. 87.4% institutional, 9.5% short, 6\u00d7 52-week range, zero analyst below $100 \u2014 crowded momentum; a single bad ESC slide = \u221230% in a day.\n6. Dilution: +11.7% share growth in 12 months + Sarepta equity stake + $181M credit facility drawn \u2192 equity holders pay for optionality.\n7. GLP-1 combination therapy makes a standalone RNAi SHTG \"pancreatitis prevention\" story a niche, not a blockbuster.\n\n**Logic combat:** Long argument strength 6.5/10; Short 5.5/10; **gap = 1.0 < 2.0 \u2192 conviction capped at Medium.** Confirmed: no new buys at $87.11.\n\n**Adversarial sources:** No live Hindenburg-style report found; the active adversarial parties are Ionis (patent case) and the credit/royalty holders (Royalty Pharma, credit facility). The 10-Q disclosure of the royalty-sale liability ($392.5M) and credit facility ($181.4M) \u2014 both absent from the vendor's \"total debt\" \u2014 are the structural red-team finds.\n\n**Killed arguments (and revival conditions):** (a) \"The 52-week low