| 0.025 | 0.770 |\n| FY35E | 2.90 | 98% | 0.285 | 2.615 | 1.050 | 0.520 | 1.045 | 0.888 | 0.120 | 0.120 | 0.020 | 0.868 |\n\nDiscount-rate derivation:\n- Risk-free rate: 4.0% [Assumption; 10Y yield [Unconfirmed]]\n- Equity risk premium: 5.0% [Assumption]\n- Beta: 1.294 [Aggregator]\n- Cost of equity: 4.0% + 1.294 \u00d7 5.0% = 10.47% \u2248 10.5%\n- Net cash position \u2192 WACC \u2248 10.5% [Assumption]\n\nTerminal value:\n- Terminal FCF growth: 3.0% [Assumption \u2014 \u2264 long-run nominal GDP]\n- TV at FY35 = $0.868B \u00d7 1.03 / (0.105 - 0.03) = $11.92B\n\nPV calculation (discount factors at 10.5%, mid-year convention for FCF, t=10 for TV):\n- PV of FCFs: FY26 -0.161; FY27 -0.367; FY28 -0.270; FY29 -0.127; FY30 0.019; FY31 0.093; FY32 0.236; FY33 0.301; FY34 0.329; FY35 0.336\n- Sum PV FCFs: $0.39B\n- PV of TV: $11.92B \u00d7 0.350 = $4.18B\n- Enterprise value: $4.57B\n- Plus net cash: $0.85B [Estimate]\n- Equity value: $5.42B\n- Per share (141.135M): $38.40\n\nExecution Value (probability-weighted optionality):\n- Sarepta milestones beyond committed payments ($10B potential): +$0.5B [Assumption]\n- Obesity program ARO-INHBE/ARO-ALK7 (Phase 1/2a; -23.2% visceral fat [Estimate \u2014 company PR via SEC]): +$0.4B [Assumption]\n- Other platform assets (CNS, MASH, future partnerships): +$0.3B [Assumption]\n- Total Execution Value: +$1.2B \u2192 +$8.50/share\n- Base intrinsic value: $38.40 + $8.50 = $46.90 \u2248 $47\n\nReverse DCF at market price $87.11:\n- Market cap $12.294B [Arithmetic]; minus net cash $0.85B \u2192 EV $11.48B\n- Implied TV = $11.48B / 0.350 = $32.8B\n- Implied terminal FCF = $32.8B \u00d7 0.075 / 1.03 = $2.39B\n- At a FY35 NOPAT margin of ~31%, implied FY35 revenue \u2248 $7.7B; at a lower WACC (9%), implied revenue \u2248 $5.1B\n- This is 1.8-2.7\u00d7 our base FY35 revenue of $2.9B. The market is pricing an SHTG peak of roughly $4.5-7B, far above Ionis\u2019s own >$2B peak guidance for Tryngolza.\nVerdict: Excessive.\n\nTornado / key variables (\u00b11\u03c3):\n1. SHTG peak sales and share (\u00b1$25/share)\n2. Sarepta milestones and obesity deal probability (\u00b1$12/share)\n3. WACC 9.25%-11.75% (\u00b1$8/share)\nTop thesis KPIs: quarterly REDEMPLO sales, sNDA filing/approval, Ionis litigation, obesity Phase 2 data.\n\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n1. Competitive response: Ionis already has Tryngolza approved in SHTG, with $108M 2025 sales and >$2B peak target [Estimate]. If REDEMPLO succeeds, Ionis will defend via pricing, contracting, and the 9,593,333 patent litigation [Estimate \u2014 FierceBiotech]. Counter-move impact: -3.\n2. Reflexivity: A high stock price improves ARWR\u2019s ability to attract talent (SBC is already a large expense), to strike partnerships, and to use equity as currency. A low price would reverse this. Current high price is a positive feedback loop, but it is priced in.\n3. Customer behavior: FCS is small (~6,500 US patients [Actual \u2014 company PR]); sHTG is the real addressable market. Early adopters will be specialist lipidologists; mainstream adoption depends on pancreatitis risk reduction, reimbursement, and dosing convenience (quarterly vs competitor monthly [Unconfirmed]).\n\nSECTION 4. SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN)\n-------------------------------------------------------------\nPrior: Engine 4 5-yr survival 40-60%; platform transition success 20-30%.\nUpdates:\n- REDEMPLO FDA approval (+likelihood)\n- SHASTA-3/4 positive (+likelihood)\n- Sarepta deal (+likelihood)\n- Ionis patent litigation (\u2212likelihood)\n- Tryngolza first-mover in SHTG (\u2212likelihood)\n- Obesity Phase 1/2a data (+likelihood, small)\n\nPosterior scenario distribution:\n\n| Scenario | Probability | Assumptions | Value/share |\n|----------|------------|-------------|-------------|\n| Bear | 30% | SHTG delayed/blocked; FCS peak $150M; Sarepta milestones minimal; obesity fails; cash burn forces dilution | $22 |\n| Base | 45% | SHTG approved FY27, captures ~15-20% of sHTG; FCS peak $300-400M; Sarepta moderate milestones; obesity option $0.4B | $47 |\n| Bull | 25% | SHTG captures 25-30%; FCS + sHTG peak $3B+; obesity partnership valued at $2B+; Sarepta milestones $1-2B | $95 |\n| Expected | 100% | Weighted | $51.50 |\n\n- Expected value: $51.50 \u2248 $52\n- Median: $47\n- 50% CI: $22-48\n- 80% CI: $22-76\n\nMargin of safety = ($51.50 - $87.11) / $51.50 = -69.1% \u2192 None.\n\nSECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n-------------------------------------------------------------\nMarket-implied horizon: at $87.11, the price embeds multi-billion-dollar SHTG and pipeline success beyond FY35 (reverse DCF implies FY35 revenue $5-8B). Our explicit forecast horizon is 3-5 years for thesis validation; on that horizon the market is paying for outcomes that, if they occur, will largely happen after Year 5. Spread = 3-5y intrinsic value minus market price = deeply negative; no positive horizon arbitrage.\n\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n-------------------------------------------------------------\nConviction score (total 15):\n1. Business quality: 2/3\n2. Valuation attractiveness: 0/3\n3. Macro alignment: 1/3\n4. Thesis clarity (measurable KPIs): 2/3\n5. Execution traceability: 2/3\nTotal: 7/15 \u2192 Medium.\n\nConviction decay: -1 per 6 months without confirming evidence (REDEMPLO sales, sNDA, litigation resolution).\n\nSizing guidelines: Medium conviction \u2192 maximum normal weight 4-6%, but with negative expected value \u2192 target position 0%.\n\nSECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n- Short interest: 9.53% of float; 9.64M shares; days-to-cover 3.39; MoM change -17.9% [Aggregator \u2014 stale as of 2026-08-08]\n- Institutional ownership: 87.38% [Aggregator \u2014 lagged]\n- Insider ownership: 3.67% [Aggregator]\n- 52-week range: $15.81-95.49; stock is at 91% of high after a >5x rally [Arithmetic]\n- Sell-side targets: low $100 / mean $110.18 / median $104 / high $126 [Aggregator \u2014 stale]\n- Sentiment: bullish/euphoric. The short-interest decline suggests a short squeeze phase rather than new bearish positioning.\nCrowding Risk Score: 9/15. Score is elevated because of the sharp run-up, high institutional ownership, and analyst targets clustering just ~20-30% above spot.\nPosition-size adjustment if ever held: -1%p.\n\nSECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n- Beta: 1.294 [Aggregator]; high correlation with biotech/growth and liquidity cycles.\n- If held in a diversified growth portfolio, a reasonable starting weight before valuation/crowding adjustments is 3-4%; after crowding adjustment, 2-3%.\n- With a negative 69% MoS and negative Kelly edge, the appropriate portfolio weight is 0%.\n- Do not pair with other high-duration small/mid-cap biotechs; ARWR would amplify the same rate/liquidity risk.\n\nSECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n-------------------------------------------------------------\nUsing scenario outcomes: 30% chance of $22, 45% chance of $47, 25% chance of $95; current price $87.11.\n- Expected wealth ratio = (0.30\u00d722 + 0.45\u00d747 + 0.25\u00d795) / 87.11 = 51.50/87.11 = 0.591 \u2192 expected return -41%.\n- Kelly fraction f* \u2248 -0.5 (negative). No position is the Kelly-optimal allocation.\n- Layer 5 and Layer 6.5 agree at 0% \u2014 no re-analysis triggered.\n\nSECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n-------------------------------------------------------------\nRisks:\n- Ionis patent litigation over US Patent 9,593,333: injunction or royalty could cap/block REDEMPLO in FCS/SHTG [Estimate \u2014 FierceBiotech]\n- Commercial execution risk: REDEMPLO FCS launch is still small; product sales are not broken out in the pack [Unconfirmed]\n- SHTG competition: Tryngolza is already marketed; Ionis is guiding >$2B peak [Estimate]\n- Regulatory delay: sNDA submission is targeted before end of 2026 [Estimate \u2014 research brief]; a 6-month PRV review is not guaranteed\n- Dilution: 1-yr share count +11.7%; 3-yr CAGR +7.7% [Arithmetic]; SBC $63-78M/yr [Filed]\n- Cash burn: TTM FCF -$0.075B [Filed]; losses widen as commercialization scales\n- Obesity program failure: Phase 1/2a data are not registrational\n\nCatalysts:\n- ESC presentation of SHASTA-3/4 (3Q 2026)\n- sNDA submission for SHTG (by end of calendar 2026)\n- FDA action with priority review (mid-2027 if filed on time)\n- Q4 FY26 earnings: first full quarter of REDEMPLO commercial data (Nov 2026)\n- Obesity program next data\n- Sarepta milestone triggers / partnership expansion\n\nSECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n- Common bear trigger across a growth portfolio: a rise in real rates or a risk-off episode. ARWR has a beta of 1.29 [Aggregator] and no earnings support until FY30E; it is effectively a long-duration asset.\n- Tail correlation: in a 2022-style regime (rates + risk-off), biotech small/mid-caps have historically drawn down 40-60% in parallel.\n- Conditional VaR estimate: 95% CVaR \u2248 -55% over a 12-month horizon [Assumption].\n- Net cash of ~$0.85B [Estimate] cushions bankruptcy risk but not mark-to-market risk.\n\nSECTION 8. MONITORING RULES\n-------------------------------------------------------------\nThesis integrity criteria (if the stock is already held):\n1. REDEMPLO net sales:\n   - Q4 FY26 (ending Sep 2026) \u2265 $25M [Assumption]\n   - Q2 FY27 \u2265 $50M [Assumption]\n   - Full-year FY27 \u2265 $250M [Assumption]\n2. sNDA accepted by FDA by 2027-03-01.\n3. FDA approval of SHTG indication by 2027-09-30.\n4. Ionis litigation: any preliminary injunction granted \u2192 thesis break.\n5. Cash + investments \u2265 $600M through FY27 10-Q.\n6. Dilution: annual share-count growth <10%.\n7. REDEMPLO gross-to-net and prescription trends disclosed quarterly.\n\nPre-mortem (failure by 2031):\nMost likely failure paths:\n- Tryngolza dominates SHTG and REDEMPLO