.84** | Jun-30 cash resources $1.567B \u2212 credit facility $0.181B \u2212 royalty liability $0.393B \u2212 Q4 burn [Actual/Arithmetic/Estimate]. |\n| 9. Unallocated platform overhead | **\u22120.60** | Discovery-stage burn not captured in options [Assumption]. |\n| **Equity value** | **7.49** | / 145M diluted [Estimate] = **$51.7/sh** |\n\n### 3.4 Cross-checks and range\n- Whole-company DCF with all company opex treated as permanent cost (fade, no options credit): **\u2248 $1.0B EV + net cash \u2192 ~$13/share** \u2014 a pessimistic floor; the framework forbids DCF-only conclusions, and this floor proves the market value lies in the options.\n- With Royalty Pharma cap (likely 1.3\u20131.5\u00d7 received amount [Unconfirmed]), base rises to **$55\u201356/share**.\n- Tornado (top-3 variables): **SHTG peak sales** ($2.4B\u2192$3.8B swings IV \u221217%/+24%); **WACC** (9%\u219212% swings \u221219%/+18%); **SHTG approval/launch timing** (6-mo slip = \u22128%). These three become thesis KPIs.\n\n### 3.5 Reverse DCF (market-implied)\nAt $87.11, EV = $11.45B. Backing out my option+SBC/drag values (~$1.3B) implies a 100%-success franchise value of ~$11.9B \u2192 **implied plozasiran peak \u2248 $5.6B** (fade model, 10% WACC, 85% approval). That is at the 60\u201370th percentile of plausible SHTG outcomes; **feasible but not base-case.**\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\n- **Competitive response (\u22121):** Ionis (Tryngolza, approved FCS) and Alnylam will defend SHTG share with pricing; GLP-1 camps (Novo, Lilly) have firepower in metabolic. Expect net-price pressure in 3\u20135 years if plozasiran's pancreatitis claim is not in the label.\n- **Reflexivity (+):** At $87, SBC is a strong talent/m&A currency (Madrigal deal at peak vibes); a drop below $40 would impair partnership leverage.\n- **Customer evolution:** FCS (advocacy, ultra-orphan, high-touch) \u2192 SHTG (cardiology/PCP; 400 \u2192 20k prescribers needed). LTV/CAC worsens; churn and polypharmacy risk rise.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\n**Prior** (Layer 1.5): platform success 20\u201330%. **Likelihood update:** SHASTA-3/4 all-endpoint success (Aug-2026), PRV acquisition, 400+ prescribers, 3 licensing deals \u2192 posterior SHTG approval = 85%; commercial peak >$2.5B = 45% [Assumption].\n\n| Scenario | Prob | Price | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Bear | 25% | **$37** | sHTG label restrictive/no pancreatitis claim; net price $60\u201380k; peak $2.0B; obesity fails; Ionis wins or injunction; financing dilution. |\n| Base | 50% | **$52** | SHTG approved mid-2027; peak $3.1B; options partially hit; dilution $400M pre-profit. |\n| Bull | 25% | **$90** | Broad label + pancreatitis claim; peak $5.5B+; INHBE partnered at $1B+; zodasiran + PNPLA3 milestones hit. |\n\n- **Expected value = 0.25\u00d737 + 0.50\u00d752 + 0.25\u00d790 = $57.75 \u2248 $58** [Arithmetic].\n- **50% CI \u2248 $47\u201370. 80% CI \u2248 $35\u201395** [Estimate].\n- **Margin of safety = (58 \u2212 87.11)/58 = \u221250% \u2192 None.**\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 4.5 \u2014 TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\nMarket price embeds a ~4\u20135-year \"success required\" horizon (SHTG launch + label breadth + pipeline). My base-case IV horizon is 3\u20135 years. **Spread \u2248 0\u20131 years \u2192 no horizon arbitrage available.** The market is not short-sighted here; it is simply more bullish on SHTG peak than my base case.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5 \u2014 CONVICTION & POSITIONING\n\n**Conviction score (15 max):** Business quality 2/3; Valuation 1/3 (negative MoS); Macro 2/3 (neutral); Thesis clarity 2/3 (KPIs measurable); Execution traceability 1/3 (commercial execution unproven, opex overrunning). **Total = 8/15 \u2192 Medium.** With 6-month decay \u22121 \u2192 **7/15 (Medium-Low).**\n\n**Sizing guideline:** Medium conviction \u2192 2\u20134% max. Engine-4 cap \u2192 start 1\u20132%. Macro neutral \u2192 no boost. Stock in \"no-MoS zone\" \u2192 actual starter = **0\u20131%**; add only at \u2264$60.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5.5 \u2014 BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\n- Short interest 9.53% of float; days-to-cover 3.39; MoM change **\u221217.9%** (shorts covering; squeeze fuel moderate) [Aggregator, 17 days stale].\n- Institutional 87.4%; insider 3.67% [Aggregator] \u2014 low insider skin-in-game.\n- 52-week range **$15.81\u201395.49** (6.0\u00d7); price near highs \u2192 sentiment hot, trend-followers long.\n- Sell-side: low $100 / mean $110 / median $104 / high $126 [Aggregator, 17 days stale] \u2014 **everyone above price; no contrarian support**.\n- Crowding risk score: **10/15** \u2192 reduce size by 1pp (already reflected in 0\u20131% starter).\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 6 \u2014 PORTFOLIO FIT\n\nARWR is a high-beta (1.29), event-driven, long-duration biotech with: low correlation to quality-compounders; moderate negative correlation to rates; positive optionality to metabolic-space re-rating. **Fits** a portfolio with <5% total speculative-biotech weights. **Poor fit** if the book already holds IONS, ALNY, or GLP-1-concentrated funds (redundant exposure). Correlation to ARKG/IBB \u2248 0.7\u20130.8 [Assumption].\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 6.5 \u2014 KELLY SIZING\n\n- Edge = (Expected value 58 \u2212 Price 87.11)/87.11 = **\u221233%**.\n- Kelly fraction = \u22120.33/(variance \u2248 3.7) \u2248 **0%** (no position).\n- Gap to Layer-5 sizing (0\u20131%) < 20pp in weight \u2014 **not a re-analysis trigger**, but a signal that the correct stance is cash/watch.\n- Action: **no new money above $65. At $55\u201360, Kelly turns positive** (EV/price \u2248 +3\u20135%) \u2192 initiate 1\u20132%; at \u2264$45, 3% max.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 7 \u2014 RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\n**Catalysts (weighted, next 12m):**\n1. ESC 2026 late-breaker (Aug 30, 2026): full SHASTA safety/suprisal detail \u2014 \u00b1$15\u201320/share.\n2. Q4 FY26 results (Nov 2026): REDEMPLO Q4 run-rate; threshold \u2265$90M/quarter \u2014 \u00b1$8\u201310.\n3. sNDA filing for SHTG (by Dec 31, 2026; PRV \u2192