SC/Phase-4 revealed a liver-fat/ALT signal that narrowed the label to \"AP-history only.\" Early warning: any ALT>3\u00d7ULN cluster. (3) The platform BD engine stalled \u2014 no new deals after Madrigal; SBC dilution 8%/yr with no offsetting partnership income. Early warning: 24 months without a new licensing agreement.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 9 \u2014 RED TEAM (ADVERSARIAL)\n\n**Short thesis (same data):**\n1. Revenue quality is low: 9M26 revenue $414.5M includes ~$200\u2013250M one-time Sarepta/Madrigal payments; product revenue is still <20% of the total.\n2. Q3 FY26 net loss \u2212$194.3M (missed; EPS \u2212$1.36 vs \u2212$1.26 y/y) [Actual]; opex $245M/qtr and compounding \u2014 the $840M net cash fund only ~2 years at this burn.\n3. One-REDEMPLO pricing won't survive SHTG: payers will not pay orphan pricing for a broad metabolic population; net price will be \u2264$100k, most likely $60\u201380k.\n4. Ionis litigation: plozasiran directly threatens Tryngolza's franchise; Ionis has deep-pocket incentive to enjoin; one adverse ruling removes the core asset.\n5. 87.4% institutional, 9.5% short, 6\u00d7 52-week range, zero analyst below $100 \u2014 crowded momentum; a single bad ESC slide = \u221230% in a day.\n6. Dilution: +11.7% share growth in 12 months + Sarepta equity stake + $181M credit facility drawn \u2192 equity holders pay for optionality.\n7. GLP-1 combination therapy makes a standalone RNAi SHTG \"pancreatitis prevention\" story a niche, not a blockbuster.\n\n**Logic combat:** Long argument strength 6.5/10; Short 5.5/10; **gap = 1.0 < 2.0 \u2192 conviction capped at Medium.** Confirmed: no new buys at $87.11.\n\n**Adversarial sources:** No live Hindenburg-style report found; the active adversarial parties are Ionis (patent case) and the credit/royalty holders (Royalty Pharma, credit facility). The 10-Q disclosure of the royalty-sale liability ($392.5M) and credit facility ($181.4M) \u2014 both absent from the vendor's \"total debt\" \u2014 are the structural red-team finds.\n\n**Killed arguments (and revival conditions):** (a) \"The 52-week low is $15.81, so $87 is rich\" \u2014 killed: the business fundamentally de-risked (approval, Phase 3 wins, partnerships); revived only if ESC data disappoint. (b) \"Sell-side mean $110 justifies entry\" \u2014 killed by reverse DCF showing $110 embeds peak >$7B; revived if label includes pancreatitis claim. (c) \"Cash is $1.57B, so no financing risk\" \u2014 killed: credit facility and royalty liability reduce net cash to $0.84B; revived if Sarepta $50M/yr + milestones extend runway into FY29.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 10 \u2014 AUDIT RESULTS\n\n**Pass: 34/37 core checks.** Key resolutions:\n- Vendor \"total cash $0.089B\" vs filed \"cash resources $1.567B\" \u2014 resolved by using the Q3-10-Q (cash + AFS securities) [Actual].\n- Vendor \"total debt $0.366B\" vs pack long-term debt column (empty) \u2014 resolved by using 10-Q credit facility $181.4M + royalty liability $392.5M, separately itemized [Actual].\n- SBC: used filed per-year series (FY25 $63M) [Actual], not vendor scalar.\n- FY24-FY25 revenue discontinuity ($4M\u2192$829M) \u2014 explained by Sarepta/Novartis upfront revenues, not a basis change [Estimate].\n- 9M26 net loss/opex: fully reconciled to 10-Q [Actual].\n**Failed/substandard (3):**\n1. **Sarepta program attribution** \u2014 could not fetch the definitive press release; identified only as \"multiple programs\"; REDEMPLO's US independence confirmed separately. \u2192 Sarepta option value is a placeholder [Unconfirmed].\n2. **Royalty Pharma terms (rate, cap)** \u2014 inferred from balance-sheet liability only; modeled 8% flat; cap adjustment noted [Unconfirmed].\n3. **Live macro rates/DXY** \u2014 not retrieved before budget exhaustion; regime distribution is [Assumption], not [Actual].\n**Bias audit:** explicit overconfidence counter \u2014 Probability-weighted EV $58 vs base SOTP $52; I used the higher $58 for MoS, a conservative bias for the \"no-buy\" conclusion. **None of the 3 failures reverses the conclusion; all three skew toward lower IV (Sarepta/N) or higher risk (royalty cap upside excluded).**\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 11 \u2014 DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n\n- **Date/T0:** 2026-08-24 | Price $87.11 | Mkt cap $12.294B.\n- **IV (probability-weighted):** $58 | Base SOTP $52\u201356 | 80% CI $35\u201395.\n- **Key assumptions:** 85% SHTG approval; $3.1B peak REDEMPLO; 10% WACC; 8% royalty-sale haircut; 0% tax through FY35; $400\u2013600M future dilution.\n- **Red-team concerns logged:** crowded positioning, Ionis injunction risk, One-REDEMPLO pricing vs payers, opex burn, SBC dilution.\n- **Trigger to re-evaluate upward:** clean ESC safety (Aug-30), Q4FY26 revenue \u2265$90M, sNDA filed by Dec-2026, Ionis dismissal.\n- **Trigger to re-evaluate downward:** any grade-3/4 liver signal, sNDA delay >6 months, gross-to-net erosion >60%, injunction.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 12 \u2014 FINAL EXECUTION OPINION\n\n**Action: HOLD \u2014 do not initiate at $87.11.**\n\nRationale: Probability-weighted fair value of ~$58 vs price $87.11 gives **no margin of safety (\u221250%)**. The market is paying for a bull SHTG outcome ($5.5B+ peak) and double my option values. The business is genuinely de-risked vs its history (approved product, positive Phase 3, $1.57B liquidity), and the bull case is real \u2014 but it is already the price.\n\n- **Conviction: Medium-Low (7/15).**\n- **Weight target: 0\u20131% now; 2\u20133% only at $55\u201360; 3% max at \u2264$45.**\n- **Strategy: staged limit orders.** Buy 1% at \u2264$60; add 1% at \u2264$50; add final 1% at \u2264$40.\n- **Catalyst-pass rule:** if ESC 2026 is clean (no new safety signal) AND Q4 FY26 REDEMPLO revenue \u2265$90M AND sNDA is filed by Dec-31-2026, re-estimate IV; a clean pass adds ~$8\u201310 to fair value, making $70\u201375 an acceptable entry.\n- **Mandatory KPI monitoring per Section 8; pre-mortem triggers set; position capped by crowding/behavioral score.**\n\n**Common-sense transla