ces):\nArrowhead is a clinical/commercial RNAi therapeutics company using its TRiM platform to silence disease-causing genes in the liver, CNS, muscle, lung, and adipose tissue. Its first approved product, REDEMPLO (plozasiran), targets APOC3 and is approved to reduce triglycerides in adults with familial chylomicronemia syndrome (FCS); it is also in Phase 3 for severe hypertriglyceridemia (SHTG). The company has monetized non-core assets to Sarepta (neuro/muscular/lung) and retains a pipeline including obesity candidates ARO-INHBE and ARO-ALK7.\nUnderstandability: Medium.\n\nMoat assessment (0-3 each):\n- Intangible assets (TRiM platform, orphan drug exclusivity, REDEMPLO label): 2\n- Switching costs (physician/patient inertia; quarterly SC dosing): 1\n- Network effects: 0\n- Cost advantage (RNAi manufacturing/biology): 1\n- Economies of scale: 1\n- Regulatory barriers (FDA approval, orphan designations): 2\n- Data moat (clinical dataset): 1\nTotal: 8/21 \u2192 Narrow Moat.\n\nMoat direction: mixed.\n- APOC3 franchise moat: Narrowing. Ionis\u2019s Tryngolza (olezarsen) is approved in sHTG and generated $108M 2025 sales / $27M Q1-2026 [Estimate \u2014 Yahoo/BioSpace]; Ionis guides >$2B peak [Estimate \u2014 Seeking Alpha].\n- TRiM platform moat: Widening \u2014 the platform now potentially targets seven cell types [Actual \u2014 company PR]; Sarepta deal validates external demand.\n\nLynch classification: Turnaround \u2192 Fast Grower transition.\n- Turnaround checkpoint: the transition from R&D to commercial is real but operating losses continue.\n- Fast-grower checkpoint: durable revenue growth not yet proven; product sales split not disclosed in pack [Unconfirmed].\n\nFinancial strength scorecard:\n- Revenue growth 5Y CAGR: +56.6% [Arithmetic \u2014 pack]\n- Revenue growth 3Y CAGR (FY22 0.243B \u2192 TTM 0.669B): ~40% [Arithmetic]\n- Operating margin latest: +11.9% [Arithmetic \u2014 FY25]; median 12-yr: -112.8% [Arithmetic]\n- ROE: -55.2% [Aggregator]\n- FCF TTM