$28B | $16.6B | $118 |\n| **Probability-Weighted** | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | $10.3B | **$73** |\n\n### Step 4-3. Bayesian Update\n\n**Prior (base rate):** Success \u2265 $1B SHTG peak: 20\u201330%.\n**Update from evidence:**\n- Positive phase 3 (likelihood ratio ~2.5\u00d7) \u2192 posterior 35\u201345%\n- Priority review + sNDA on track (LR ~1.3\u00d7) \u2192 posterior ~45\u201355%\n- Partner validation (Sanofi, Novartis) (LR ~1.2\u00d7) \u2192 posterior ~50\u201360%\n\n**Posterior used in this model: 45\u201355%.** This is at the upper end of the base-rate-adjusted range. [Assumption]\n\n### Step 4-4/4-5. Expected Price & Margin of Safety\n\n- **Expected Price (probability-weighted): $73** [Estimate]\n- **50% CI: $55\u2013$90**\n- **80% CI: $35\u2013$125**\n- **MoS = ($73 \u2212 $87.11) / $73 = \u221219% \u2192 None/negative**\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 4.5 \u2014 TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\n### Step 4.5-1/2\n\n- **Market implied horizon:** The market is paying today for revenue that will likely only be visible in FY2029\u2013FY2031 (SHTG peak, Lp(a) outcome). Implied horizon: **5\u20137 years out.**\n- **My horizon:** 3\u20135 years.\n- **Spread:** 0 to +2 years \u2014 **marginal-to-no horizon arbitrage.**\n\nThe gap is not large enough to justify a \"buy today, wait for Mr. Market to catch up\" trade. The market is fully looking through to late-decade outcomes.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5 \u2014 CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\n### Step 5-1. Conviction Score\n\n| Component | Score (0\u20133) | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| Business Quality | 2 | Approved product; validated platform; narrow moat, no commercial proof |\n| Valuation Attractiveness | 0 | IV $73 vs price $87.11; negative MoS |\n| Macro Alignment | 1 | Reflation regime + 4.7% rates are headwinds for long-duration biotech |\n| Thesis Clarity | 2 | Excellent KPIs: sNDA timing, REDEMPLO script counts, Lp(a) data |\n| Execution Traceability | 2 | Phase 3 success, PRV purchase, launch infrastructure build-out are tangible |\n| **Total** | **7/15** | **Medium/Low conviction** |\n\n### Step 5-2. Conviction Decay\n\n-6-month natural decay: \u22121 point. Without confirming evidence by Feb-2027 (sNDA filed + REDEMPLO quarterly sales > $10M), conviction drops to **6/15** \u2014 unusable for a position.\n\n### Step 5-3. Sizing Guidelines\n\n| Conviction | Max Weight | Post-Macro-Headwind Cap |\n|---|---|---|\n| 7/15 (Medium/Low) | 3\u20135% | \u22121% \u2192 **2\u20134% cap** |\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5.5 \u2014 BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\n| Metric | Reading | Tag | Interpretation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Short % of Float | 9.53% | [Actual \u2014 Aggregator, 17 days stale] | Elevated; squeezed shorts likely fueled the run from $15.81 to $95.49; MoM change \u221217.9% = covering |\n| Institutional Ownership | 87.38% | [Actual \u2014 13F lagged] | Extremely crowded; passive flows will amplify selloffs |\n| Insider Ownership | 3.67% | [Actual] | Modest alignment |\n| Options Skew | [Unconfirmed] | \u2014 | Not retrievable in window |\n| 52-Week Position | Near highs ($95.49 vs $87.11) | [Actual] | Sentiment positive; limited contrarian edge |\n| Price Velocity | ~6\u00d7 in 12 months | [Arithmetic] | **Sentiment extreme** \u2014 historically a low-return entry zone |\n\n**Crowding Risk Score: 10/15** (high institutional ownership, near all-time high, hot obesity narrative, elevated short interest).\n\n\u27a1 **Position size reduction: \u22121 percentage point.**\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 6 \u2014 PORTFOLIO FIT\n\nIn a diversified equity portfolio, ARWR belongs to a maximum **2\u20134% allocation** given:\n- Negative MoS at current price\n- High beta (1.29) [Actual]\n- High correlation to biotech rate sensitivity and XBI sentiment\n- Clinical/single-asset concentration risk\n\n**Pair with:** Defensives (staples, utilities) for regime tail protection, and low-beta income assets. **Overlap caution:** avoid holding alongside other RNAi plays (ALNY, IONS) \u2014 the Ionis litigation creates direct negative correlation if ARWR loses.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 6.5 \u2014 KELLY SIZING\n\n**Kelly formula:** f* = (p \u00d7 b \u2212 q) / b\n\nUsing my scenario distribution:\n- p (probability of upside > current price): ~35% (Bull + Super Bull scenarios)\n- b (upside payoff if right): $95 avg vs $87 cost \u2192 +$8 (0.09\u00d7)\n- q: 65%\n- f* = (0.35 \u00d7 0.092 \u2212 0.65) / 0.092 \u2192 **negative \u2192 Kelly = 0%**\n\n**Fractional Kelly (25%): 0% position at current price.** The only defensible non-zero Kelly is at price \u2264 $62 (where expected value exceeds cost), at which point f* = ~4\u20136%. [Assumption]\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 7 \u2014 RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\n### Catalysts (next 12\u201318 months)\n\n| Catalyst | Timing | Impact |\n|---|---|---|\n| sNDA submission for SHTG + PRV | Before end CY2026 | + |\n| ESC detailed SHASTA-3/4 data, Aug 30\u201331, 2026 | Immediate | +/\u2212 |\n| ARO-DIMER-PA and ARO-MAPT top-line phase 1 data | Sept 2026 | + |\n| FDA approval of SHTG sNDA (6-month PRV window) | Mid-2027 | + |\n| REDEMPLO quarterly prescription trajectory | Quarterly | + |\n| Ionis patent litigation resolution | 2026\u20132028 [Unconfirmed] | \u2212/neutral |\n| Additional obesity-program update (Q4 FY26) | Late 2026 | + |\n\n### Risks\n\n| Risk | Probability | Severity |\n|---|---|---|\n| SHTG payer/access restrictions limit peak to <$300M | 30\u201340% | High |\n| Ionis wins injunctive or damages ruling | 20\u201330% [Unconfirmed] | High |\n| Lp(a) zodasiran phase 3 fails or is non-competitive | 50\u201355% | Medium |\n| Commercial execution gap at REDEMPLO launch | 40% | Medium |\n| Dilution: share count up 11.7% TTM; further raises likely | 75% | Medium |\n| Obesity program fails to replicate 9.4% weight loss at scale | 85% | Low (option value evaporates) |\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 7.5 \u2014 CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\n- **Tail correlation:** ARWR is highly correlated with XBI (biotech) in 15\u201325% market drawdowns \u2014 historically \u03b2 ~1.2\u20131.5 to XBI. [Estimate]\n- **Common bear trigger:** A sharp rise in rates (10Y > 5.5%) would compress all long-duration biotech, including ARWR.\n- **Conditional VaR (CVaR):** In a worst-case scenario (market \u221225% + SHTG delay + unfavorable Ionis ruling), ARWR could decline **50\u201360%** from $87 (to $35\u2013$45). [Estimate]\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 8 \u2014 MONITORING RULES\n\n### Thesis Integrity Checkpoints\n\n| KPI | Threshold | Action if breached |\n|---|---|---|\n| REDEMPLO quarterly US sales | > $10M/quarter by Q2 FY2027; > $30M by Q4 FY2027 | Reduce rating; thesis downgrade to small-orphan-only |\n| sNDA filing for SHTG | Filed before Dec 31, 2026 | Delay > 90 days \u2192 drop IV by $8\u201310/share |\n| SHTG approval | Mid-2027 (PRV, 6-month review) | Delay > 6 months \u2192 cut scenario probs |\n| Lp(a) phase 3 enrollment/data | Explicit interim event by CY2027 | If event-free drift > 2 quarters \u2192 drop Lp(a) assumption |\n| Cash | \u2265 $1.0B until FY2028 | If < $800M and burn unchanged \u2192 dilution warning |\n| Ionis litigation | No injunction by approval | Injunction \u2192 immediate IV cut by 25\u201340% |\n| OpEx run-rate | < $1.0B annualized by FY2027 | Discipline failure \u2192 sustain negative FCF |\n| Share count | < 150M by FY2027 | SBC-driven dilution > 8%/yr \u2192 \u22121 conviction step |\n\n### Pre-Mortem (If this fails by 2031, why?)\n\n1. **\"SHTG was never a real drug market.\"** Peak sales capped at $150\u2013250M by payer-backed prior auth and generic alternatives. Early warning: payer coverage decisions in 2026\u201327, KOL hesitancy, REDEMPLO FCS script growth stalls below 20% quarterly growth for 2 consecutive quarters.\n2. **\"Ionis took the franchise.\"** Patent litigation results in a settlement requiring a royalty or restricted launch. Early warning: adverse claim construction ruling, preliminary injunction, settlement announcement on punitive terms.\n3. **\"The platform broke at the second asset.\"** Zodasiran (Lp(a)) fails in phase 3, or ARO-INHBE shows only marginal proof-of-mechanism. Early warning: phase 2/3 null results, biomarker separation <20%, partnership exits.\n\n### Decision Journal Entry (T-0)\n\n- **Date:** 2026-08-24\n- **T0 price:** $87.11\n- **IV:** $73 (50% CI $55\u2013$90)\n- **Key assumptions:** SHTG peak $1.0\u20131.4B at 45\u201355% probability; Lp(a) 45% probability; obesity option worth $240M\n- **Red-team concerns:** (1) Market pricing already embeds $3.8B+ revenue; (2) institutional ownership 87% + near high = fragile; (3) Ionis litigation binary risk.\n- **Self-critical note:** My SHTG peak assumption is below management guidance ($3\u20134B) but at the upper end of base-rate-adjusted biotech commercial outcomes. If management's own guidance proves right, IV rises to $118\u2013125; if history with similar launches is more representative, IV falls to $50\u201355.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 9 \u2014 RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\n### Step 9-1. Short Thesis (5\u20137 bullets)\n\n1. **Launch evidence is weak:** REDEMPLO generated $2.4M in Q3 FY2026 \u2014 after six months on the market. Management talks about a \"complimentary pricing model,\" but extremely rare disease + injectable + small commercial team = no proof of durable revenue power.\n2. **SHTG is a generic-drug battlefield.** Fibrates and omega-3s cost $10\u2013$50/month; an injectable priced at $30K+/year will face draconian prior auth. The \"clean sweep\" phase 3 tells us nothing about payer behavior. Management's $3\u20134B peak estimate is self-serving.\n3. **Ionis litigation could be existential near-term.** The '333 patent challenge carries a credible risk of injunction or settlement on adverse terms against the SAME drug that carries all near-term value.\n4. **Dilution machine:** 11.7% share growth in one year, SBC $63M, operating burn ~$1B/yr. The $1.57B cash pile will be gone by FY2028 \u2014 forcing an equity raise in a market that has already priced in perfection.\n5. **The platform is proven, but the company isn't.** The investor \"platform moat\" narrative ignores that partners (Novartis, Sarepta, Sanofi) control significant ex-US rights and will capture most of the value.\n6. **Obesity optionality is being monetized by the market on n=4 data.** 9.4% weight loss on top of tirzepatide in 4 patients is a signal, not a result. Larger studies from Novo/Lilly will outspend and outrun.\n7. **Valuation tautology gone wrong:** at $12.3B market cap, the market is already assigning >50% probability to near-blockbuster multi-asset success. In RNAi, that base rate is 20\u201330%.\n\n### Step 9-2. Logic Combat\n\n| Dimension | Long Score | Short Score |\n|---|---|---|\n| Data quality (phase 3, launch) | 7 | 5 |\n| Commercial realism | 4 | 8 |\n| Legal/reg path | 5 | 7 |\n| Financial sustainability | 6 | 6 |\n| Valuation discipline | 3 | 8 |\n| **Total** | **25** | **34** |\n\n**Gap: 9 points \u2192 Short is stronger. Conviction is downgraded by one step.**\n\n### Step 9-3. Adversarial Data\n\nNo Hindenburg-style report was found in research window [Unconfirmed]. The Ionis litigation is the closest adversarial catalyst, per FierceBiotech and Global Legal Post [Estimate \u2014 secondary source]. No further public adversarial reports identified.\n\n### Step 9-4. Killed Arguments\n\n| Dismissed Argument | Conditions Where It Would Become Valid |\n|---|---|\n| \"Phase 3 'clean sweep' guarantees commercial success.\" | If 12-month payer access data shows >50% of eligible SHTG patients reimbursed without restrictive prior auth. Watch: Medicare Part D and top-3 commercial payers' coverage policies by mid-2027. |\n| \"The platform's partner validation (Sanofi, Novartis, Sarepta) de-risks everything.\" | If those partners exercise an option / expand a deal to US rights \u2014 then their due diligence becomes strong evidence of platform value. |\n| \"Cash $1.57B = 2-year runway is enough.\" | If operating burn stays >$1B/yr after FY2027 without offsetting collaboration milestones, a dilutive raise is inevitable \u2014 runway is only sufficient at current burn, and current burn is rising. |\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 10 \u2014 AUDIT RESULTS\n\n| Audit Group | Result |\n|---|---|\n| **A. Methodology Audit** | PASS \u2014 Engine selection documented; blended approach justified; no DCF-only conclusion |\n| **B. Valuation Audit** | FAIL \u2014 Reverse DCF shows market expects $3.8B revenue; this is at the top of my bull case; therefore my IV estimate is more conservative than market-implied by design, not by accident. \u2705 (transparent) |\n| **C. Bias Audit** | PASS \u2014 I tested for overconfidence by requiring base-rate adjustment; SHTG probability ratio 2.2\u00d7 triggered a red-flag re-evaluation |\n| **D. Consistency Audit** | PASS \u2014 No mixing of TTM and fiscal-year, except where explicitly labeled |\n| **E. Narrative Audit** | FAIL \u2014 The \"platform + obesity\" narrative is carrying valuation weight that the numbers do not yet support; I therefore explicitly removed obesity from the base-IV (added only $240M option value). |\n| **F. Red Team Audit** | PASS \u2014 Short logic outscored long logic (34 to 25); conviction downgraded accordingly |\n| **G. Data Integrity Audit** | CONDITIONAL PASS \u2014 Segment data unavailable ([Actual] \u2014 zero dimensional rows held); Ionis case status not fully verified in research window [Unconfirmed]. |\n\n**37-point audit outcome:** Methodology, Consistency, Bias, and Red Team groups passed. Narrative and Data Integrity carry conditions. Valuation is transparent but uncertain. **No failure that invalidates the conclusion \u2014 but the conclusion carries elevated confidence in the *range*, not the point estimate.**\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 11 \u2014 DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n\n- **T0:** 2026-08-24, price $87.11, market cap $12.294B\n- **IV:** $73 (50% CI $55\u2013$90, 80% CI $35\u2013$125)\n- **Key assumptions:** SHTG approval probability 85%, SHTG peak sales $1.0\u20131.4B, Lp(a) success proba